+# Aegis — App Store & Apple Ecosystem Compliance Guidance (Artifacts)
+
+This module supplies code and runbooks to reduce App Store friction and address privacy/regulatory risk when integrating Aegis with Apple devices.
+
+What this patch includes:
+- CI workflow (macOS) to build sample app, convert/validate Core ML models and optionally submit for notarization.
+- Notarization + evidence bundle scripts to produce artifacts for App Review.
+- Presidio redaction wrapper to ensure PII/PHI is redacted at ingest.
+- Enhanced Consent Manager with fine-grained scopes and revocation.
+- Fetchtoken mint/redeem service and on-device client to support offline approvals.
+- Core ML quantization helper and guidance to produce smaller, on-device optimized models.
+- DP utilities to apply simple Gaussian noise for aggregated telemetry / federated updates.
+- Swift SDK stubs for consent, retrieval, fetchtoken, prefilled A2A UI and Secure Enclave signing hooks.
+
+Recommended operator steps to integrate with App Store flows:
+1. Produce an evidence bundle for each app + model promotion that includes:
+   - MLflow run IDs and perf metrics (latency, size, emissions)
+   - Notarization ticket and code-signing certificate references
+   - Rekor / cosign attestations for server artifacts
+   - Privacy & consent policy references and consent schema
+2. Use on-device processing via Core ML whenever feasible to minimize PII and regulatory surface area.
+3. For regulated domains (health, biometrics), prefer local processing, strong redaction (Presidio) and require retrieval + A2A for any original data leaving device.
+4. Document data flows clearly for App Review (how consent is obtained, how data is retained, how takedowns are handled).
+5. Use Secure Enclave for device receipts and provide server‑side verification endpoints.
+
+Developer adoption & CI templates:
+- Use the macOS CI workflow to validate Core ML artifacts on macOS runners before promoting.
+- Provide an Xcode Swift Package containing the SDK stubs in services/ios/sdk so developers can drop-in consent/approval flows.
+- Offer sample app & CI configs that demonstrate notarization + evidence bundle generation for App Review.
+
+Privacy & security reminders:
+- Keep Apple credentials secure (use GitHub Secrets or CI secret stores), and prefer manual notarization for initial approvals.
+- Use Vault Transit for signing and KMS for encryption of originals, do not store private signing keys in repo.
+- For DP and federated learning, tune epsilon according to privacy policy and use rigorous DP libraries for production.
+
